    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Source+Sans+3:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;0,700;0,800;1,400;1,600&family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=Permanent+Marker&display=swap"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Nav />

    <div data-zoom-group data-zoom-scan>
      <section class="hero-banner">
        <img data-tilt src={img('01.webp')} alt="Two SureCall EZ-5G Signal Test app screens on a green background, showing a signal-strength check and the SureCall wordmark" />
      </section>
      <section class="marquee-section" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="marquee-row">
          <div class="marquee-track marquee-track-left">
            {[...marqueeWords, ...marqueeWords].map((w) => <span>{w}</span>)}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="marquee-row">
          <div class="marquee-track marquee-track-right">
            {[...marqueeWords, ...marqueeWords].map((w) => <span>{w}</span>)}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="marquee-row">
          <div class="marquee-track marquee-track-left">
            {[...marqueeWords, ...marqueeWords].map((w) => <span>{w}</span>)}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="marquee-row">
          <div class="marquee-track marquee-track-right">
            {[...marqueeWords, ...marqueeWords].map((w) => <span>{w}</span>)}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="marquee-phone">
          <div class="phone-frame">
            <video class="phone-video" src={`${base}images/surecall/opening.mp4`} autoplay muted loop playsinline aria-label="SureCall app opening screen with an animated signal waveform"></video>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="head-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="head-top">
            <h1 class="title">SureCall</h1>
            <div class="context-box">
              <p class="context-label">Where this started</p>
              <h2 class="context-heading">A booster in the wrong spot does not improve the signal</h2>
              <p>SureCall builds cell signal boosters and worked with Verizon on a phone app that helps people figure out where to put one. The app does three things: it tests the signal where you are standing, it confirms the booster is working once it is mounted, and it explains enough about 5G UW that the numbers mean something. People use it in a garage or a crawlspace, so it had to be <strong>fast, readable, and hard to get wrong</strong>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <dl class="meta">
            {meta.map((m) => (
              <div>
                <dt>{m.label}</dt>
                <dd>{Array.isArray(m.value) ? m.value.map((v) => <span>{v}</span>) : m.value}</dd>
              </div>
            ))}
          </dl>

          <p class="intro">Boosters go into garages, basements and rural houses where the signal was already bad. Two kinds of people install them and they want different things. Technicians do this all day and want the raw signal number. Homeowners do it once and want to be told they are finished. I had to give the homeowner a plain answer without slowing the technician down. Verizon wanted fewer support calls, and <strong>most support calls come from someone who could not tell whether the booster was working</strong>.</p>

          <p class="pull-quote" data-typewriter>
            <span aria-hidden="true"><span class="tw-seg" data-full="How do you tell somebody "></span><span class="tw-seg pull-quote-highlight" data-full="the install actually worked"></span><span class="tw-seg" data-full=", without teaching them what dBm means?"></span></span>
            <span class="sr-only">How do you tell somebody the install actually worked, without teaching them what dBm means?</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="stat-band">
        <div class="location-block">
          <p class="location-label">Project Location</p>
          <p class="location-name">Silicon Valley, California</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="dark-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="challenge-head">
            <span class="quirky quirky-blue">Signal data</span>
            <h2>Nobody knows what minus 80 dBm means, including me at first</h2>
          </div>
          <ol class="challenge-grid">
            {challenges.map((c, i) => (
              <li class="challenge-card" data-tilt>
                <span class="challenge-num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
                <p>{c}</p>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>I never spoke to a user, and I am not going to pretend I did</h2>
          <p>I did not run my own research on this project. I worked from a brief written by the SureCall and Verizon project managers. It said three things: customers do not know what counts as a good or bad dBm value, <span class="callout-phrase">people want to "see it work" before they believe it</span>, and instructions have to be <strong>skimmable, with the detail underneath</strong>. We built two personas from that brief so I had a specific person in mind while drawing each screen. Those personas told me what SureCall and Verizon believed about their customers. That was the only information I had, and it was better than designing for myself.</p>
          <p class="take">I had no research of my own, but I did have a user, described in the brief. I think student work usually either invents findings it never collected or designs for nobody in particular. <strong>I wrote down what I was assuming instead, so someone could check it.</strong> Every decision on this page comes from a line in that brief.</p>
          <div class="image-row image-row-personas">
            <img data-tilt src={img('03.webp')} alt="User persona: Sarah Scott, 38, a remote marketing worker in Wisconsin installing her first signal booster, with her goals, pain points, and needs from the app" />
            <img data-tilt src={img('04.webp')} alt="User persona: Jamal Ortiz, 29, a field technician in Texas who installs boosters professionally, with his goals, pain points, and needs from the app" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>I sketched first, because a sketch is quick to throw away</h2>
          <p>I sketched rough concepts to work out <strong>the flow, the screens, and which features were worth keeping</strong>. Sketches are fast to draw and easy to lay side by side, and I would rather throw out six sketches than one prototype.</p>
          <p class="take">Client work changed how I sketch. When a client is paying you, there is pressure to bring something finished, and if you finish it too early you spend the meeting defending it instead of testing it. So I started bringing three rough options instead of one finished one. <strong>People will tell you a rough drawing is wrong, and that is what the meeting is for.</strong></p>
          <div class="image-row-single image-row-single-wide">
            <img data-tilt src={img('07.webp')} alt="Low-fidelity wireframes for the SureCall app" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow-label">Deciding what stays on the screen</p>
          <p>This page only has to tell you whether the install worked. For every element on it I asked whether it helped answer that question, or whether it was only there to look thorough. <strong>Most of them did not answer it, so I removed them.</strong></p>
          <p class="take">I think deciding what to take off a screen is harder than deciding what to put on it. Adding is easy and it feels productive, because you can justify each thing you add on its own. <strong>I have never regretted taking something off a screen, and I have regretted keeping things on nearly every project I have worked on.</strong></p>
          <div class="image-row-single image-row-single-wide">
            <img data-tilt src={img('09.webp')} alt="Two iteration options for the signal-test page: Option 1 with Test Again and Learn More buttons, and Option 2 showing an automatic rescan with a Close button" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="image-row-single image-row-single-wide">
            <img data-tilt src={img('08.webp')} alt="Three iteration options for explaining 5G C-Band and UW technology: plain information with no aesthetic, relevant information in a gradient bubble, and relevant information with color coded signal specifics" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="feature-band">
        <div class="feature-media">
          <img data-tilt src={img('13.webp')} alt="Two SureCall screens showing the signal search state and the color coded Great signal-strength result" />
        </div>
        <div class="feature-text">
          <h2 class="feature-heading">Showing the word Good instead of minus 80 dBm</h2>
          <p>A color coded meter with plain labels ("Good", "Great") translates the signal reading, so nobody has to learn what dBm means to find out whether they are done. The app <strong>rescans on its own once the booster is mounted</strong>, because that is the moment you want the number. The raw RSRP value stays on the screen for the technician who wants the real reading. Both people get what they need from the same screen, without switching modes.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="feature-band feature-band-reverse">
        <div class="feature-media">
          <img data-tilt src={img('14.webp')} alt="Three SureCall screens guiding a user to move near a window, checking 5G UW strength, and offering booster tips" />
        </div>
        <div class="feature-text">
          <h2 class="feature-heading">You should know the booster works before you climb down the ladder</h2>
          <p>The test finishes in a few seconds, so you are not standing on a ladder wondering whether to take the booster back down. These installs happen in the worst rooms in the house, so <strong>a clear pass or fail mattered more than a detailed readout</strong>. Nobody standing in a dark garage is going to read much.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow-label">The finished prototype</p>
          <div class="image-row-single image-row-single-phone">
            <video class="prototype-video" src={`${base}images/surecall/prototype.mp4`} autoplay muted loop playsinline aria-label="Walkthrough of the final SureCall prototype, from the signal-strength check through booster setup"></video>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow-label">The design kit</p>
          <div class="image-row-single image-row-single-wide">
            <img data-tilt src={img('12.webp')} alt="SureCall design kit: typography scale, color palette, and logo and icon assets" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="white-block white-block-flush-bottom">
        <div class="image-row-single">
          <img data-tilt src={img('02.webp')} alt="Collage of SureCall app screens arranged at an angle, showing the signal test, booster setup, and information flows" />
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>How it turned out, and what I would change</h2>
          <p>On this project I learned to design for the room the app is used in as well as for the screen. Bad light, a ladder, and one free hand: designing for those conditions made me cut things I liked, including a detailed signal history screen that nobody standing on a ladder is going to read.</p>
          <p>Working at a small company meant I was involved in every step. The part I valued most was sitting with the backend engineers and watching what actually gets built. They told me to change things based on <strong>how easy or hard an element was to code</strong>, which was humbling at first and then just useful. Thank you to SureCall for having me.</p>
          <p>What I learned here was how to work when the research belongs to someone else. I had a brief, two project managers and no users, and I had to decide which lines in that brief I was willing to build on. Most client work is like that, and no class had asked me to do it.</p>
          <p>I was nervous for most of it. It was the first time I designed something a company was actually going to ship, and I spent the first few weeks expecting someone to tell me I did not know what I was doing. <strong>That went away once I stopped treating the brief as a test I could fail and started using it as the description of the user I had.</strong> I left more confident than I arrived, which I had not expected.</p>
          <h2 class="ai-heading">How I would change this today with AI</h2>
          <p>The app tells you the signal is weak. It does not tell you what to do about it. Today I would let someone describe their house in plain words, or take a photo of the room, and have a model suggest where to mount the booster and where to put the outside antenna. That is what every support call is actually asking, and right now the app leaves it to the person standing on the ladder.</p>
          <p>I would keep the live reading as the thing people trust. The brief said customers want to see it work before they believe it, and a sentence written by a model is not proof. <strong>The model can suggest where to try next. The meter still has to be the thing that tells you that you are done.</strong></p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2 class="takeaways-heading">What I learned</h2>
          <div class="takeaways-grid">
            {takeaways.map((t) => (
              <div class="takeaway-card">
                <span class="takeaway-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <h3>{t.title}</h3>
                <p>{t.body}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="up-next">
        <div class="wrap">
          <span class="quirky quirky-blue">Up Next</span>
          <a class="up-next-row" href={nextProject.href} data-tilt>
            <img src={nextProject.image} alt="" />
            <div>
              <h2>{nextProject.title}</h2>
              <p>{nextProject.subtitle}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="btn-outline">View Project</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <Footer />

    <Lightbox />

    <script>
      import '../../scripts/site.js';
      import '../../scripts/lightbox.js';

      const btn = document.querySelector('[data-copy-email]');
      btn?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText('julianliaowork@gmail.com');
          const original = btn.textContent;
          btn.textContent = 'Copied!';
          setTimeout(() => { btn.textContent = original; }, 1500);
        } catch {
          window.location.href = 'mailto:julianliaowork@gmail.com';
        }
      });

      // Belt-and-suspenders: the autoplay/muted/loop/playsinline attributes
      // already handle this in every modern browser, but some browsers
      // silently drop a programmatic play() if it's called before the
      // element is attached — this re-triggers it once the page is ready.
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLVideoElement>('.phone-video, .prototype-video').forEach((v) => {
        v.play().catch(() => {});
      });

      // Typewriter effect on the pull-quote — types each segment in order
      // (plain text, then the highlighted phrase, then the trailing plain
      // text) once the quote scrolls into view. Reduced-motion and
      // no-IntersectionObserver both fall back to showing the full text.
      const quoteEl = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-typewriter]');
      if (quoteEl) {
        const segments = Array.from(quoteEl.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.tw-seg'));
        const reduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

        const typeSegments = () => {
          let segIndex = 0;
          let charIndex = 0;
          const step = () => {
            if (segIndex >= segments.length) return;
            const seg = segments[segIndex];
            const full = seg.dataset.full ?? '';
            if (charIndex <= full.length) {
              seg.textContent = full.slice(0, charIndex);
              charIndex++;
              setTimeout(step, 28);
            } else {
              segIndex++;
              charIndex = 0;
              setTimeout(step, 28);
            }
          };
          step();
        };

        if (reduced || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) {
          segments.forEach((seg) => { seg.textContent = seg.dataset.full ?? ''; });
        } else {
          const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries, obs) => {
            entries.forEach((entry) => {
              if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                typeSegments();
                obs.disconnect();
              }
            });
          }, { threshold: 0.4 });
          io.observe(quoteEl);
        }
      }
    </script>

    <style>
      :global(body) {
        background: #ffffff;
      }

      .wrap {
        max-width: 74rem;
        margin-inline: auto;
        padding-inline: clamp(1.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
      }

      /* Nav ------------------------------------------------------------ */

      .btn-pill {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        border: 1px solid var(--ink);
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 0.6em 1.4em;
        text-decoration: none;
        color: var(--ink);
        background: transparent;
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 600;
        cursor: pointer;
      }

      .btn-pill-solid {
        background: var(--ink);
        color: var(--bg);
      }

      /* Hero banner ------------------------------------------------------- */
      .hero-banner {
        aspect-ratio: 8 / 3;
        overflow: hidden;
      }

      .hero-banner img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        object-fit: cover;
        object-position: center;
      }

      /* Marquee ----------------------------------------------------------- */
      .marquee-section {
        position: relative;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        justify-content: space-around;
        min-height: clamp(380px, 48vw, 640px);
        padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
        overflow: hidden;
        background: #ffffff;
      }

      .marquee-row {
        overflow: hidden;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }

      .marquee-track {
        display: inline-flex;
        width: max-content;
      }

      .marquee-track span {
        display: inline-block;
        padding-inline: 1.5rem;
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 4.2vw, 2.6rem);
        color: #4fd8ae;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }

      .marquee-row:nth-child(odd) .marquee-track span {
        color: rgba(79, 216, 174, 0.55);
      }

      .marquee-track-left {
        animation: marquee-left 32s linear infinite;
      }

      .marquee-track-right {
        animation: marquee-right 32s linear infinite;
      }

      @keyframes marquee-left {
        from { transform: translateX(0); }
        to { transform: translateX(-50%); }
      }

      @keyframes marquee-right {
        from { transform: translateX(-50%); }
        to { transform: translateX(0); }
      }

      .marquee-phone {
        position: absolute;
        top: 50%;
        left: 50%;
        transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
        z-index: 5;
      }

      .phone-frame {
        width: clamp(140px, 16vw, 220px);
        aspect-ratio: 658 / 1396;
        border: 3px solid var(--ink);
        border-radius: 1.5rem;
        padding: 0.5rem;
        background: var(--bg);
      }

      .phone-frame .placeholder {
        height: 100%;
        aspect-ratio: auto;
        border-radius: 1rem;
      }

      .phone-video {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        object-fit: cover;
        border-radius: 1rem;
      }

      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .marquee-track-left,
        .marquee-track-right {
          animation: none;
        }
      }

      /* Head block -------------------------------------------------------- */
      .head-block {
        padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
      }

      .head-top {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 1.5rem;
        align-items: start;
        margin-bottom: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
      }

      .title {
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 6rem);
        letter-spacing: var(--track-tight);
        line-height: 0.98;
        color: var(--ink);
        margin: 0;
      }

      /* Fill matches the section background on purpose — the reference
         had this as a plain white box floating on the page's cream
         background, which read as a mismatched card rather than part
         of the page. */
      .context-box {
        background: transparent;
        border-left: 3px solid var(--line-strong);
        padding-left: 1.25rem;
      }

      .context-label {
        margin: 0 0 var(--gap-label);
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: var(--step-small);
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
        color: var(--ink-faint);
      }

      .context-heading {
        margin: 0 0 var(--gap-subheading);
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: 1.3rem;
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .context-box p:not(.context-label) {
        margin: 0;
        max-width: none;
        font-size: var(--step-body);
        line-height: var(--leading-body);
        color: var(--ink-soft);
      }

      @media (min-width: 800px) {
        .head-top { grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; }
      }

      .meta {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(10rem, 1fr));
        gap: 1.5rem;
        padding-bottom: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
        margin: 0 0 clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
      }

      .meta dt {
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-size: var(--step-small);
        color: var(--ink-faint);
        margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
      }

      .meta dd {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 600;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
        font-size: var(--step-caption);
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .meta dd span {
        display: block;
      }

      .intro {
        max-width: none;
        font-size: var(--step-body);
        line-height: var(--leading-body);
        color: var(--ink-soft);
      }

      .pull-quote {
        position: relative;
        max-width: none;
        font-family: var(--font-serif);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.4vw, 2.4rem);
        line-height: 1.4;
        color: var(--ink-faint);
        margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
        text-align: center;
      }

      .pull-quote-highlight {
        color: #06251e;
        font-weight: 600;
        box-shadow: inset 0 -0.35em 0 rgba(0, 179, 133, 0.22);
      }

      .pull-quote[data-typewriter]::after {
        content: '';
        display: inline-block;
        width: 2px;
        height: 1em;
        margin-left: 2px;
        background: currentColor;
        vertical-align: text-bottom;
        animation: pull-quote-blink 0.9s steps(1) infinite;
      }

      @keyframes pull-quote-blink {
        50% { opacity: 0; }
      }

      .sr-only {
        position: absolute;
        width: 1px;
        height: 1px;
        padding: 0;
        margin: -1px;
        overflow: hidden;
        clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
        white-space: nowrap;
        border: 0;
      }

      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .pull-quote[data-typewriter]::after {
          animation: none;
        }
      }

      /* By the numbers ------------------------------------------------------- */
      .stat-band {
        background: #00b38a;
        color: #fdfbf9;
        padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
      }

      .location-block {
        text-align: center;
        padding-inline: clamp(1.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
      }

      .location-label {
        margin: 0 0 var(--gap-label);
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: var(--step-small);
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
        color: #fdfbf9;
      }

      .location-name {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
        line-height: 1.1;
        color: #fdfbf9;
      }

      /* Dark / white blocks ---------------------------------------------- */
      .dark-block {
        background: var(--ink);
        color: var(--bg);
        padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
      }

      .white-block {
        padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
      }

      .white-block-flush-bottom {
        padding-bottom: 0;
      }

      .white-block h2 {
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
        letter-spacing: var(--track-tight);
        margin: 0 0 var(--gap-heading);
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .dark-block h2 {
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
        letter-spacing: var(--track-tight);
        margin: 0 0 var(--gap-heading);
      }

      .white-block p {
        max-width: none;
        font-size: var(--step-body);
        line-height: var(--leading-body);
        color: var(--ink-soft);
      }

      .dark-block .wrap > p {
        max-width: none;
        font-size: var(--step-body);
        line-height: var(--leading-body);
        color: rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.7);
      }

      /* Typographic emphasis: bold only. Bold marks a design decision,
         and .callout-phrase (used once, on the single clearest insight on
         the page) is the same bold at full ink. The earlier italic and
         colored-phrase treatments were removed — body copy carries no
         emphasis other than weight. */
      .white-block strong,
      .context-box strong,
      .feature-text strong {
        color: var(--ink);
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .dark-block strong {
        color: var(--bg);
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .callout-phrase {
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .eyebrow-label {
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 600;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
        color: #00b385;
        margin: 0 0 var(--gap-eyebrow);
        font-size: var(--step-small);
      }

      /* Images ------------------------------------------------------------ */
      .image-row {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 1.5rem;
        margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
      }

      .image-row img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
      }

      @media (min-width: 700px) {
        .image-row-personas { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
      }

      .image-row-single {
        margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
      }

      .image-row-single-wide {
        max-width: 56rem;
        margin-inline: auto;
      }

      .image-row-single img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
      }

      .image-row-single-phone {
        max-width: 20rem;
        margin-inline: auto;
      }

      .prototype-video {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        aspect-ratio: 912 / 1800;
        border-radius: 1.5rem;
      }

      .placeholder {
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        aspect-ratio: 21 / 9;
        border: 1px dashed var(--line-strong);
        background: #ffffff;
        color: var(--ink-faint);
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }

      .placeholder-phone {
        aspect-ratio: 9 / 19;
      }

      /* Feature bands (green, full-bleed) --------------------------------- */
      .feature-band {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        background: #00b38a;
      }

      .feature-media img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        object-fit: cover;
      }

      .feature-text {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        justify-content: center;
        padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
      }

      .feature-heading {
        font-family: var(--font-serif);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.1rem);
        color: var(--ink);
        margin: 0 0 var(--gap-heading);
      }

      /* Fill matches the section background on purpose — same fix as the
         context box above; the reference had a white card sitting on
         this green band. */
      .feature-text p {
        margin: 0;
        max-width: none;
        font-size: var(--step-body);
        line-height: var(--leading-body);
        color: rgba(6, 37, 30, 0.75);
      }

      @media (min-width: 800px) {
        .feature-band { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
        .feature-band-reverse .feature-media { order: 2; }
        .feature-band-reverse .feature-text { order: 1; }
      }

      /* Challenge cards --------------------------------------------------- */
      .challenge-head {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 1.1rem;
        margin-bottom: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
      }

      .challenge-head .quirky {
        margin-top: -0.2rem;
      }

      .challenge-head h2 {
        color: var(--bg);
        margin: 0;
      }

      .quirky {
        font-family: var(--font-quirky);
        font-size: 1.2rem;
        transform: rotate(-3deg);
        display: inline-block;
      }

      /* All three challenge sections (and Up Next) share one accent now —
         SureCall's own brand green (#00B385, from the Design Kit asset)
         instead of the earlier blue/sage/coral rotation. */
      .quirky-blue,
      .quirky-sage,
      .quirky-coral {
        color: #00b385;
      }

      .challenge-grid {
        list-style: none;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 1rem;
      }

      /* Every card carries the lit treatment. There used to be three copies
         of this grid, each dimming all but one card; the dim state read as
         disabled rather than as sequence, so the grid appears once now and
         all of it is legible. */
      .challenge-card {
        --tilt-x: 0deg;
        --tilt-y: 0deg;
        border: 1px solid rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.3);
        border-left: 3px solid #00b385;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        background: rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.08);
        transform: perspective(700px) rotateX(var(--tilt-x)) rotateY(var(--tilt-y));
        transition: background 0.3s ease, border-color 0.3s ease, transform 0.3s var(--ease-out);
      }

      .challenge-card p {
        margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
        max-width: none;
        color: var(--bg);
        font-weight: 500;
        font-size: var(--step-body);
        line-height: var(--leading-body);
      }

      .challenge-num {
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 800;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        color: #00b385;
      }

      @media (min-width: 700px) {
        .challenge-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
      }

      /* Key takeaways ------------------------------------------------------- */
      .takeaways-heading { color: var(--ink); }

      .takeaways-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 1.5rem;
        margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
        padding-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      }

      .takeaway-card {
        padding-left: 0;
      }

      .takeaway-dot {
        display: inline-block;
        width: 24px;
        height: 24px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: #00b385;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
      }

      .takeaway-card h3 {
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: var(--step-card-title);
        color: var(--ink);
        margin: 0 0 var(--gap-subheading);
      }

      .takeaway-card p {
        margin: 0;
        max-width: none;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        font-size: var(--step-body);
        line-height: var(--leading-body);
      }

      @media (min-width: 700px) {
        .takeaways-grid {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        }

        .takeaways-grid .takeaway-card:last-child {
          border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
          padding-left: 2rem;
        }
      }

      /* Up next --------------------------------------------------------------- */
      .up-next { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem); }

      .up-next-row {
        --tilt-x: 0deg;
        --tilt-y: 0deg;
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 1.5rem;
        margin-top: 1rem;
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      .up-next-row img {
        width: 100px;
        aspect-ratio: 1;
        object-fit: cover;
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        transform: perspective(700px) rotateX(var(--tilt-x)) rotateY(var(--tilt-y));
        transition: transform 0.3s var(--ease-out);
      }

      .up-next-row h2 {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.2rem);
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .up-next-row p {
        margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
        color: var(--ink-faint);
        font-size: var(--step-caption);
      }

      .btn-outline {
        margin-left: auto;
        border: 1px solid var(--ink);
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 0.5em 1.2em;
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: var(--step-small);
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      /* Footer ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
      .footer { text-align: center; }

      .footer-heading {
        color: var(--bg);
        font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
      }

      .footer-actions {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 1rem;
        margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
      }

      .footer .btn-pill { border-color: var(--bg); color: var(--bg); }
      .footer .btn-pill-solid { background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); }

      .footer-social {
        color: rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.7);
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 600;
        text-decoration: none;
      }
    
      /* Opinion asides — my running commentary on each stage, set apart
         from the account of what happened. */
      .take {
        max-width: 60ch;
        margin: 2rem 0 2rem;
        padding-left: 1.1rem;
        border-left: 3px solid #00b385;
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-size: var(--step-body);
        line-height: var(--leading-body);
        color: var(--ink-soft);
      }

      .take strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

      .ai-heading { margin-top: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.25rem); }
</style>
  </body>
</html>
